{"duration_api_ms":34927,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0bfcf637-9bc9-4f3d-aaa0-5f7d7477720a","total_cost_usd":0.18611919999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12080,"cache_read_input_tokens":106396,"output_tokens":3408,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1092},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12080,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1088,"cache_read_input_tokens":25962,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1410,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1410},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":3408,"cacheReadInputTokens":106396,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12080,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.18611919999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1092,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":12080,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Devon's triage doesn't hold up. The bug is in `OutputPHPFilter`, the lexer is behaving correctly, and `OutputPythonFilter` is not affected. Do not close this as `VERDICT_NOT_AFFECTED`.\n\n**Where each claim goes wrong**\n\n1. **\"`OutputPHPFilter` already escapes the dangerous characters.\"** It doesn't. `sqlparse/filters/output.py:120` escapes only `\\` and `\"`. The GHSA comment at lines 116–118 covers breaking out of the string with a backslash before a quote, and says nothing about `$`. The filter wraps its output in a PHP double-quoted string (lines 93, 108, 126), and PHP expands `$var`, `${expr}` and `{$obj->prop}` inside those strings. I ran the current code and got:\n   - `$sql = \"SELECT '${system($_GET[x])}'\";`\n   - `$sql = \"SELECT '\\\\$name'\";` — PHP reads `\\\\` as a literal backslash, so `$name` still expands.\n2. **\"The lexer misclassifies `$name`.\"** It doesn't. `'$name'`, `'${…}'` and `'{$obj->prop}'` all lex as one `Token.Literal.String.Single`. `$body$text$body$` lexes as a dollar-quoted literal (`keywords.py:20-35`), and a bare `$name` is `Name.Placeholder` (`keywords.py:137`), which is also correct. The filter turns every token into text no matter its type (lines 119–123), so changing the lexer couldn't fix this.\n3. **\"`OutputPythonFilter` has the same `$` risk.\"** It doesn't. It writes a plain single-quoted Python string (line 45), not an f-string, so `$` and `{}` mean nothing there. Line 69 escapes `\\` and then `'`, which is the right set. I ran `exec()` on the Python output for all six payloads and each one came back identical to the input SQL.\n\n**Root cause:** `OutputPHPFilter._process` puts SQL text inside a PHP double-quoted string without escaping `$`.\n\n**Minimal fix** (`sqlparse/filters/output.py:120`, one line, nothing else changes):\n\n```python\ntoken.value = token.value.replace('\\\\', '\\\\\\\\').replace('\"', '\\\\\"').replace('$', '\\\\$')\n```\n\nBackslashes must be escaped **first**. If `$` were escaped first, the backslash pass would turn `\\$` into `\\\\$`, and PHP would expand the variable again. I tested the fix by patching it in memory (no files changed):\n\n- `\"SELECT '\\${system(\\$_GET[x])}'\"`\n- `\"SELECT '{\\$obj->prop}'\"`\n- `\"SELECT \\$body\\$text\\$body\\$\"`\n- `\"SELECT '\\\\\\$name'\"`, which PHP reads back as `\\$name`\n- Multi-line output with `.=` still works.\n\nPHP isn't installed here, so I haven't run the output through a real PHP interpreter. That and a regression test are still needed.\n\nIf you'd like, I can apply the one-line fix and add tests for these payloads plus a PHP round-trip check, to run wherever PHP is available.","ttft_ms":1721,"type":"result","duration_ms":35416,"uuid":"0209ea77-7acd-471a-8f6e-3bb437fb8099","ttft_stream_ms":1464,"time_to_request_ms":224,"first_content_frame_ms":1464,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-23T22:59:00.503Z"}

